# Inspecting open source software

When you need the source of open source software, clone it into `~/src`. Do not clone it into the current workspace. Do not ask first.

Use `gh repo clone OWNER/REPO ~/src/REPO`.

```bash
gh repo clone psf/requests ~/src/requests
```

If `~/src/REPO` already exists, use that checkout.

For remotes `gh` cannot clone, use `git clone URL ~/src/REPO`.
